1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
This is a plan Claude Code executed on its own. Nineteen nodes. One evening.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:15,000
It follows Felix Rieseberg's method: altitude, depth, range.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:24,000
A node is not done because the model says so. It needs a proof. Only I can validate.

4
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Three agents, three ways to speed up a parser, each in its own branch, scored by the same benchmark.

5
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Then I ran the benchmark myself. 334 ms down to 44.

6
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Cost and time on screen before and during. Estimates calibrated against real timings.

7
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:58,000
In auto mode, after each turn, the plugin hands Claude the next open node.

8
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:06,000
And I steer from anywhere. Validate, go deeper, go wider, prune.

9
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Ambiflex. Open source, one line to install.
